AC unit tests / regression suite
================================

Runnable suite emits **DejaGnu / GCC `.sum` style** results (PASS/FAIL +
Summary).

Layout
------
Sources live in `src/unittest/` (formerly `demo/`). Classic Amiga `ccx`
samples (`hello.c`, `Sieve.c`, …) share this directory.

Amiga (from `src`)
------------------
  make demo-self2
  unittest-out/ac-self2/ac_tests

Or build and run in one step:

  make demo-run-self2

Also: `make demo-ac`, `make demo-self`, `make demo`
(aliases: `unittest-ac`, `unittest-self`, `unittest-self2`).

Host (from `src/ac`)
--------------------
  make test
  make -f src/unittest/Makefile check CC=./AC \
    DEMODIR=src/unittest OUTDIR=src/unittest/out/host

What gets built
---------------
- `unittest-out/<cc>/*.s` — compile-only smokes for each `test_*.c`
- `unittest-out/<cc>/ac_tests` — linked DejaGnu driver (`ac_tests.c`)
- `unittest-out/<cc>/cli/` — command-line option smoke outputs

CLI options: `make demo-cli-self2` (also runs as part of `make demo-self2`).
See `cli_opts.txt`.

Classic samples: `make -f src/unittest/Makefile classic` (Amiga `ccx`).

Example output
--------------
  PASS: smoke/global_answer
  PASS: literal/binary_or
  FAIL: some_test (got 0 want 1)
  ...
                === ac unittest Summary ===

  # of expected passes            28
  # of unexpected failures        0
  # of untested testcases         2

Exit status 0 = all PASS; 1 = any FAIL.
